{"parentUuid":"69739661-a66e-45c1-b02e-e940df9e3b89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"gen-1784227808-eMkeIgpqdmzKQgK6j0mV","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **`bench.mjs`** — your eval runner. Summary of what it does:\n\n- Calls **OpenRouter** (`/api/v1/chat/completions`) over a set of models × prompts\n- Defaults to `z-ai/glm-5.2` and `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`\n- For each (model, prompt, repeat) run, records to:\n  - `results/results.csv` — run_id, timestamp, model, prompt, token usage, cost, latency, a manual `pass` column\n  - `responses/<run_id>.txt` — the raw model response (for manual grading)\n- Flags: `--models`, `--prompts`, `--n` (repeats)\n- Requires `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` env var; no deps beyond Node 18+\n\nA few things worth noting if you're iterating on this:\n\n1. **`pass` is filled manually** — there's no automated grading. The `responses/` files exist so a human reads and scores them.\n2. **Cost handling is best-effort** — pulls `usage.cost ?? body.cost`, else blank (\"fill via dashboard\").\n3. **Runs are sequential** (`for...for...for` with `await`) — fine for small matrices, but it doesn't parallelize, so `--n` repeats × many prompts × 2 models will be slow.\n\nWant me to do anything specific — e.g., add automated grading, parallelize runs, add more models, or look at the existing `results.csv`?","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":36864,"output_tokens":326,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Alibaba"},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8e071d8b-04f9-4df7-8e05-9d7c89026e38","timestamp":"2026-07-16T18:50:17.659Z","session_id":"ba837ca2-9